{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFour Python test modules under `tests/unit/review_bot` contain 5 audited prose blocks with repetition, held-out-test boilerplate, or historical framing. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@50716c9aed87479e4347a4daf084c9778c8793f7`; the stable IDs below, not mutable line numbers, are the edit allowlist.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the five allowlisted true leading docstrings. Capture immutable before/final blobs for every owned path and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only an allowlisted `Expr(Constant(str))` that is the first statement of a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining normalized ASTs to match.\n\nTokenize both blobs and reject every changed inline comment or non-allowlisted full-line comment. Preserve runtime strings, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, test data, and exact shebang/directive physical lines. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_decision_auth_heldout.py`\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_voter_casts_no_vote_when_decision_auth_is_blank`\n- `tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_rotation_heldout.py`\n  - `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_startup.py`\n  - `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_token_nonleak_heldout.py`\n  - `D:<module>`\n\n`D:<symbol>` means the true leading docstring owned by that module/function. No other docstring or comment in these files is editable.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Decision auth is validated before provider/job work; blank/whitespace auth fails closed with no vote or fallback principal, while an otherwise-clean PASS path remains the positive control.\n- The composed provider-native `LLMRuntime` reaches the actual request runner without an ambient replacement.\n- A startup binding is an immutable per-process snapshot; a fresh compose observes rotated policy; each operation gets a fresh snapshot.\n- Partial/rejected telemetry credentials disable telemetry fail-open without changing operation results.\n- Inbound bearer/OAuth material cannot enter `OperationSnapshot`; secret/non-JSON leaves are rejected and canonical snapshot bytes contain no ambient token.\n- These modules are collected directly by pytest. No `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found at the pinned base.\n\nPreserve these complete directive-bearing physical lines byte-for-byte:\n\n```python\nfrom test_review_bot import FakeGerrit, _event, _patch_review  # type: ignore\n        binding.policy = {}  # type: ignore[misc]\n        binding.llm_runtime = LLMRuntime()  # type: ignore[misc]\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Changes are limited to the five stable-ID docstrings and adjacent blank lines; the normalized-AST and token/comment comparisons pass for every owned path.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter while retaining its listed current contract; held-out copy/run boilerplate, repetition, and ornamental emphasis are removed.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the edits posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [ ] All five TSV rows cite immutable blobs and record `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing/failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] Focused pytest, scoped Ruff check/format, comment hygiene, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_decision_auth_heldout.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_rotation_heldout.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_startup.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_token_nonleak_heldout.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/ruff check tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_decision_auth_heldout.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_rotation_heldout.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_startup.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_token_nonleak_heldout.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/ruff format --check tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_decision_auth_heldout.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_rotation_heldout.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_startup.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_token_nonleak_heldout.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `git diff --check -- tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_decision_auth_heldout.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_rotation_heldout.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_startup.py tests/unit/review_bot/test_rp04_s5_token_nonleak_heldout.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788618381107730001,"uuid":"19d01481-f1a6-4277-b092-3f66df4adbe5"}